{
  "id": "s02-l06b",
  "unit": "s02-consonants",
  "title": "Consonants 6b: শ ষ স হ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Three letters, one sound.** শ, ষ and স are normally all `sh`: শিক্ষক (`shikkhok`), মানুষ (`manush`), সকাল (`shokal`, morning). স becomes a real `s` in clusters before t, n, r, l (স্টেশন `steshon`).\n\nYou can't hear which one a word uses, so learn it as part of the spelling. Shape tips: **শ** is the common one; **ষ** has a slash through its middle and rarely starts a word; **স** has an open curl.\n\n**হ** is a plain h: হাত (`hat`, hand), হ্যাঁ (`hya~`, yes).",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-sha",
      "bn": "শ",
      "tr": "sho",
      "en": "sh as in 'shop'",
      "notes": "Name: talobbo sho (তালব্য শ). The most common sh letter (শিক্ষক)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ssa",
      "bn": "ষ",
      "tr": "sho",
      "en": "sh as in 'shop' (same sound as শ)",
      "notes": "Name: murdhonno sho (মূর্ধন্য ষ). Same sound as শ; spelling only. Rarely starts a word; common in the middle (মানুষ)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-sa",
      "bn": "স",
      "tr": "sho",
      "en": "sh, or s before t / n / r / l",
      "notes": "Name: donto sho (দন্ত্য স). Usually 'sh' (সকাল shokal), but 's' in clusters like স্ত, স্ক (s04)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ha",
      "bn": "হ",
      "tr": "ho",
      "en": "h as in 'hat'",
      "notes": "Name: ho (হ). Changes shape with some vowel signs: হু, হৃ (s03-l02)."
    },
    {
      "id": "hat",
      "bn": "হাত",
      "tr": "hat",
      "en": "hand"
    }
  ],
